+ * object. A null 'this' or a class not yet initialised leaves the trace AT the call: the interpreter then makes the real call, which
+ * throws / initialises exactly as before. The AOT code of such a method is that load too (the same IL), and the return value lands in the
+ * return slot the way do_jit_call leaves it (small integers widened to 32 bits by the stencil, as do_jit_call's epilogue does). The
+ * verdict per callee is worked out on an interpreter thread (it reads metadata) and kept; the compiler thread only reads it. */
